# .dockerignore
#
# Tells Docker which files to EXCLUDE from the build context.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS:
#   When you run `docker compose build`, Docker sends the entire build context
#   (the project directory) to the Docker daemon. Without .dockerignore, it
#   would send the .venv (can be 1GB+), .git history, .chroma data, etc.
#   This would make every build slow and the images unnecessarily large.
#
#   By ignoring these paths, the build context is kept small, builds are fast,
#   and sensitive files like .env never get baked into the image layer.

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The .venv is for local development. Inside Docker, Poetry installs packages
# directly into the system Python (virtualenvs.create = false).
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ── Python cache files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are regenerated at runtime and should never be in an image.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
*$py.class

# ── Git history ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Git metadata has no place in a runtime container.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# ── Environment file ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IMPORTANT: Never bake .env into a Docker image!
# API keys baked into images can leak if the image is pushed to a registry.
# We pass .env via `env_file:` in docker-compose.yml instead.
.env
.env.*

# ── ChromaDB data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The .chroma directory is mounted as a bind volume in docker-compose.yml.
# We don't need it in the image — it's mapped from the host at runtime.
.chroma/

# ── Generated audio output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Same as .chroma — mounted as a volume, not baked into the image.
outputs/

# ── IDE and OS files ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Poetry cache ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local Poetry cache from development — not needed in the container.
.cache/

# ── Test and coverage artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.tox/
*.cover

# ── Documentation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log

# ── Docker files themselves ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dockerfiles and docker-compose configs have no place in the running container.
# NOTE: docker-entrypoint.sh is intentionally NOT excluded — Dockerfile.api
#       COPYs it into the image as the container ENTRYPOINT script.
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml

# ── Test suite ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tests run in CI, not inside the production container.
tests/
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
